Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: modload_load_given()'s refusal of a name the cache already holds: the bytes given are cached beside the old ones and dlopen()ed by the same path, and libdl hands back the object it loaded first -- a module that runs which is not the one given.  modload_test's [6] gives modload_b/twin.so's bytes as modload_a/twin.so, which [1] cached, and gets modload_a's twin back.
Run: --iommu intel --edu --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: modload_test: \[6\] modload_b/twin.so.s bytes given as modload_a/twin.so, which is cached: gave modload_a/twin.so A, where a refusal was asked for; modload_a/twin.so gives modload_a/twin.so A -- WRONG

diff --git a/uros/src/lib/libmodload/modload.c b/uros/src/lib/libmodload/modload.c
index bc7c2e8d..1ff06091 100644
--- a/uros/src/lib/libmodload/modload.c
+++ b/uros/src/lib/libmodload/modload.c
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@ modload_load_given(const char *class, const char *name, vm_offset_t data,
 	 * A module of that name in the cache would be the one dlopen() reads,
 	 * and not the one given: refused, not chosen between.
 	 */
-	if (find_cached_module(class, name) != NULL) {
+	if (0 && find_cached_module(class, name) != NULL) {
 		printf("%s: \"%s/%s\" is in the cache already: the module "
 		       "given is not loaded\n", log_tag, class, name);
 		return NULL;
